From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmime: tracks keep and play their data (sysex, lyrics, tempo, time signature, marker, parameter control, segment trigger, wave, tool graph Load), Clone / PlayEx / Join / GetParamEx

The DirectMusic tracks of dmime had stubs which returned S_OK without
looking at their arguments or keeping any data. They now keep what they
load and behave as the DirectMusic documentation and the conformance tests
describe:

- Init, InitPlay and EndPlay of tracks which keep no play state are plain
  S_OK (their FIXMEs sat on correct answers). The tempo track's play state
  now remembers the performance, EndPlay without state is E_POINTER.
- Clone: E_POINTER without result, E_INVALIDARG for a negative or inverted
  range, a new track with the items of the range moved to start at zero
  (the tempo and time signature in effect at the start are carried over).
- PlayEx: E_POINTER without performance, otherwise the reference times are
  converted through the performance and handed to Play.
- Sysex track: loads its 'syex' items and plays DMUS_SYSEX_PMSG messages.
  Lyrics track: keeps the events and plays DMUS_LYRIC_PMSG messages.
  Time signature track: GetParam(GUID_TimeSignature) with the time relative
  to the asked time and the next change, Play sends DMUS_TIMESIG_PMSG,
  Disable/EnableTimeSig make GetParam return DMUS_E_TYPE_DISABLED.
  Tempo track: Play sends DMUS_TEMPO_PMSG followed by DMUS_PMSGT_DIRTY,
  GetParamEx/SetParamEx convert through the performance, Join, the
  tempo disable flag. Marker track: loads 'vals' and 'play' and answers
  GUID_Valid_Start_Time and GUID_Play_Marker. Sequence track: frees its
  items. Segment trigger track: Play starts the loaded segments with
  PlaySegmentEx. Wave track: Download / Unload / auto download parameters.
  Parameter control track: loads its objects, parameters and curves
  (Play has no DMO to apply them to and validates its arguments only).
  GetParamEx/SetParamEx of the tracks which have no extended parameters
  return the same unsupported codes as GetParam / SetParam.
- Tool graph: IPersistStream::Load creates the tools of its DMTL forms,
  lets them load their data and inserts them at their index.
- Sequence, sysex and the other tracks' E_NOTIMPL answers for parameters,
  notification types, Compose and Join are what the conformance tests
  expect and are left alone.

The todo_wine marks of the track tests which pass now are removed.
